module j3.gfx.canvas
    Draw RGBA8 game art in memory, without a window or SDL. Pixel mode is crisp;
    Smooth mode gives circles and lines one pixel of edge coverage. Coordinates
    start at the upper left. Keep the Arena alive while using the Canvas.
    Any thread, on an arena you own: its tables are read-only (`j3c doc threads`).

enum Mode
    Rasterization and texture filtering style.
    Pixel
    Smooth

struct Color
    Straight-alpha RGBA color; channels are 0..255.
    r: u8
    g: u8
    b: u8
    a: u8

fn rgb(r: u8, g: u8, b: u8): Color
    Opaque color.
fn rgba(r: u8, g: u8, b: u8, a: u8): Color
    Color with alpha.
struct Canvas
    A mutable, tightly packed RGBA8 image. Pixels are top row first.
    pixels: []u8
    w: i32
    h: i32
    mode: Mode
    fn Canvas.create(arena: &Arena, w: i32, h: i32, mode: Mode): Canvas
        Allocate one 8-byte-aligned image buffer. Maximum is 268,435,455 pixels.
    fn Canvas.clear(this: &Canvas, color: Color)
        Replace every pixel, including alpha.
    fn Canvas.pixel(this: &Canvas, x: i32, y: i32, color: Color)
        Composite one pixel. Out-of-bounds coordinates are ignored.
    fn Canvas.fillRect(this: &Canvas, x: i32, y: i32, w: i32, h: i32, color: Color)
        Fill a clipped rectangle; opaque colors use a direct row loop.
    fn Canvas.strokeRect(this: &Canvas, x: i32, y: i32, w: i32, h: i32, thick: i32, color: Color)
        Draw a rectangle border inward from its edges.
    fn Canvas.gradientRect(this: &Canvas, x: i32, y: i32, w: i32, h: i32, start: Color, end: Color, vertical: bool)
        Fill an axis-aligned rectangle with a horizontal or vertical gradient.
    fn Canvas.noiseRect(this: &Canvas, x: i32, y: i32, w: i32, h: i32, seed: u32, cell: i32, low: Color, high: Color)
        Deterministic two-color noise. `cell` controls block size (minimum 1).
    fn Canvas.blit(this: &Canvas, source: Canvas, dx: i32, dy: i32)
        Composite a source image at an integer destination. Source must be distinct.
    fn Canvas.savePng(this: Canvas, path: string, arena: &Arena): Result<int, IoError>
        Export RGBA8 PNG: unfiltered rows, one fixed-Huffman DEFLATE block with greedy LZ77, so a
        flat-shaded picture is tens of kilobytes instead of `w * h * 4` bytes.
    fn Canvas.fillCircle(this: &Canvas, cx: f32, cy: f32, radius: f32, color: Color)
        Fill a circle. Pixel mode uses exact coverage; smooth mode softens the edge.
    fn Canvas.strokeCircle(this: &Canvas, cx: f32, cy: f32, radius: f32, thick: f32, color: Color)
        Draw a circle border of `thick` pixels.
    fn Canvas.line(this: &Canvas, ax: f32, ay: f32, bx: f32, by: f32, thick: f32, color: Color)
        Draw a line with round caps and a positive thickness.
    fn Canvas.fillTriangle(this: &Canvas, ax: f32, ay: f32, bx: f32, by: f32, cx: f32, cy: f32, color: Color)
        Fill a triangle, clipping to the image. Smooth mode antialiases edges.

fn diff(a: &Canvas, b: &Canvas, tol: int, out: &Canvas): int
    Count pixels where any channel of `a` and `b` differs by more than `tol`, and draw them
    red in `out` (every other pixel at 25% grey). All three must be the same size, else -1.
fn inflate(z: []u8, out: []u8, arena: &Arena): bool
    Inflate the zlib stream `z` into exactly `out`. False on bad or short data.
fn decodePng(bytes: []u8, arena: &Arena): Canvas
    Decode an 8-bit, non-interlaced PNG (gray, RGB, palette, gray+alpha, RGBA) to RGBA8.
    Returns a canvas with `w == 0` when the bytes are not one of those. The Rust side
    (`j3c/src/png.rs` `decode`) is the same algorithm; fix both together.
fn loadPng(path: string, arena: &Arena): Canvas
    `decodePng` of a file; `w == 0` when it is missing or unsupported.
